<div class="flex max-w-md flex-col gap-8">
  <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
    <h2 class="font-body text-sm font-semibold text-muted-foreground">Command palette</h2>

    <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
      Press <kbd class="rounded-well border border-border bg-offset px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs">⌘K</kbd>
      (or <kbd class="rounded-well border border-border bg-offset px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs">Ctrl K</kbd>
      on Windows/Linux) anywhere on this page to open it, or use the button below.
      Type to filter, <kbd class="rounded-well border border-border bg-offset px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs">&uarr;</kbd>/<kbd class="rounded-well border border-border bg-offset px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs">&darr;</kbd>
      to move between results, and <kbd class="rounded-well border border-border bg-offset px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs">&crarr;</kbd> to open the highlighted one.
    </p>

    <%= render AtomicView::Components::ButtonComponent.new(nil, "Open command palette", {
      variant: :outline,
      onclick: "document.getElementById('example-command-palette').showModal()"
    }) %>

    <%= render AtomicView::Components::CommandPaletteComponent.new(
      id: "example-command-palette",
      sections: [
        {
          label: "Pages",
          results: [
            {label: "Dashboard", href: "#dashboard", hint: "G D"},
            {label: "Reservations", href: "#reservations", hint: "G R"},
            {label: "Settings", href: "#settings"}
          ]
        },
        {
          label: "Actions",
          results: [
            {label: "Create new park", href: "#new-park", hint: "⌘N"},
            {label: "Invite teammate", href: "#invite"}
          ]
        }
      ]
    ) %>
  </section>

  <section class="flex flex-col gap-2">
    <h2 class="font-body text-sm font-semibold text-muted-foreground">Host app setup</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
      The gem cannot register a controller into a host app's own Stimulus
      <code>Application</code> instance. Add this to the host app's
      <code>app/javascript/controllers/index.js</code>:
    </p>
    <pre class="overflow-x-auto rounded-btn border border-border bg-offset p-3 text-xs"><code>import CommandPaletteController from "atomic_view/controllers/command_palette_controller"
application.register("atomic-view--command-palette", CommandPaletteController)</code></pre>
    <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
      Once registered, <code>Cmd/Ctrl+K</code> opens the dialog from
      anywhere on the page -- the controller listens for it on
      <code>document</code>, so no trigger element is required (a button
      like the one above is just a discoverable alternative). Results are
      passed as plain data (see <code>CommandPaletteComponent</code>'s
      class docs for the shape); the controller filters rows client-side as
      the user types and supports arrow-key navigation + <code>Enter</code>
      to activate the highlighted result.
    </p>
  </section>
</div>
